# Secure codegen

- Never commit secrets, `.env`, keys, or tokens; never put them in packs or run logs.
- Validate and sanitize untrusted input at API boundaries.
- Mutating endpoints: authenticate + authorize (tenant/company/role) before side effects.
- Use parameterized queries / safe ORM binders — no string-built SQL.
- Escape/sanitize user content on web; least-privilege CORS and actuators.
- Log structured errors without passwords, JWTs, or unnecessary PII.
- For `security: elevated`, run `story-security` and require human merge.
- Prefer updating `.agentic/security/` ledger when findings appear.
